<!--
    INFR3120 - Assignment 2
    Projects Page

    This page displays seven projects from my IT studies.
    Bootstrap cards are used to organize the projects
    in a responsive layout.
-->

<!-- Loads the shared header and navigation bar -->
<%- include('partials/header', { title: 'Projects' }) %>
<!-- Bootstrap container centers the Projects page content -->
<main class="container my-5">

    <h1 class="text-center mb-3">My Projects</h1>

    <p class="text-center mb-5">
        These projects highlight my experience in cybersecurity,
        cloud technologies, databases, web development,
        research, and technical problem solving.
    </p>
<!--
    Bootstrap grid organizes the projects into rows.
    The g-4 class adds spacing between project cards.
-->
    <div class="row g-4">

        <!-- Project 1 -->
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">
                        CRM API Security Risk Assessment
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-muted">Informatica Industry Capstone</p>
                    <p>
                        Worked with Informatica as part of a
                        six-member team examining security and
                        privacy risks in CRM extensions.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        As Team Lead, I contributed to risk
                        evaluation, vendor assessments,
                        data-flow analysis, and security
                        recommendations.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 2 -->
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">
                        AI Fitness Glasses Security Policy
                    </h3>
                    <p>
                        Collaborated with a team to develop
                        a security policy and risk assessment
                        for hypothetical AI-powered fitness glasses.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Examined biometric data, wireless
                        connections, cloud services, device
                        software, and AI-related risks using
                        ISO 27005 principles.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 3 -->
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="card h-100 shadow-sm">
                <div class="card-body">
                    <h3 class="card-title h5">
                        BooksInc Database Web Application
